==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Puppetmaster Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Puppetmaster & Charley''' when obtained from [[Revenge of A-Cyclone (Deadly)|Revenge of A-Cyclone]] (guaranteed to drop) and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Clockwork Cat is a nice [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] to be added into your team. However, his [[Slow|slow]] chance is only a mere 20%, meaning it is not that reliable. To remedy this, he is given a good attack rate and animation making his [[Special Abilities|ability]] happen more often. His high movement speed is somewhat detrimental if you are using other Cats with slower movement speed, as he is likely to run into enemy attacks without other units able to catch up and defend him.

==='''True Form'''===
Puppetmaster & Charley gets improved range, slow duration, and slow chance. The range is increased from 200 to 225. The main selling point of this [[True Form]] however, is the increased slow time going from 2.67 seconds to a whopping '''6 seconds!''' Combined with this unit's fast attack rate, [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies can be left slowed for a long time! The slow chance is also increased to 30%. A stack of Puppetmaster & Charley can use these improvements to keep the likes of Super Metal Hippoe and even [[Sir Metal Seal]] at bay. Sadly, he still retains his Single Attack, meaning that a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Panties Cat (Special Cat)|Lollycat]] or a [[Volley Cat (Rare Cat)|Curry Cat]] may be more useful in most situations.

